{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Projection.Reflection","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Linear"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dH_verticalReflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dH_verticalReflection","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryReflection.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**C1 — reflection in a vertical plane preserves the hyperbolic distance.**\nDERIVED from the conformal-height-scaling engine (`IsDHIsometry.dH_eq`) at\n`lam ≡ 1`: norms and height both scale by `1`, so the line element `‖v‖/z` is\npreserved, and the reflection is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflection_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflection_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryReflection.lean#L79-L81","doc":"The vertical reflection is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflectionIsom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflectionIsom","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryReflection.lean#L41-L77","doc":"**The conformal height-scaling data of the vertical reflection** (`lam ≡ 1`).\nThe reflection is a Euclidean isometry, so its derivative — itself, as a linear\nmap — scales every norm by `1`; and it fixes the height coordinate, so the height\nscales by `1` too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.verticalReflection","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryReflection.lean#L35-L39","doc":"The vertical coordinate plane `{x = 0}`, as the subspace orthogonal to the\nfirst basis vector `e₀ = single 0 1`.  Reflection across it negates `x` and fixes\n`(y, z)` — a vertical-plane reflection (it contains the height axis `e₂`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}